type":"text","text":"generation is raised only for a change an older peer cannot skip; the new generation then gets a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session application protocol of its own beside the current one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"App versions travel as text and compare as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireVersion"},{"type":"text","text":". A host that no longer serves a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device’s version says so with a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/Goodbye"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/Goodbye\/update"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"TLS-and-pinning","text":"TLS and pinning"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireTLS","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" builds the TLS options for both ends. Each side presents a self-signed P-256","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"certificate (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/WireIdentity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") and pins the other’s key by its fingerprint, the SHA-256 of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SubjectPublicKeyInfo (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireWire\/documentation\/HeadwireWire\/SPKI","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Trust is decided entirely by that pin; names, dates, and chains","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are never evaluated. Session tickets and resumption are off, so a removed device can’t return on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an old ticket.","type":"text"}]